# Component Code Structure

## Section Separators
Use clear section separators to organize component code:

```typescript
export class MyComponent {
    // ----------------------------------------
    //        Injected Services
    // ----------------------------------------
    private readonly router = inject(Router);
    private readonly service = inject(DataService);

    // ----------------------------------------
    //        Inputs
    // ----------------------------------------
    @Input({ required: true }) data!: DataType;
    @Input({ required: false }) label?: string;

    // ----------------------------------------
    //        Outputs
    // ----------------------------------------
    @Output() saved = new EventEmitter<void>();

    // ----------------------------------------
    //        Properties
    // ----------------------------------------
    protected loaded = false;
    private internalState: string[] = [];

    // ----------------------------------------
    //        Lifecycle
    // ----------------------------------------
    ngOnInit(): void { /* ... */ }

    // ----------------------------------------
    //        Public Methods
    // ----------------------------------------
    protected handleClick(): void { /* ... */ }

    // ----------------------------------------
    //        Private Methods
    // ----------------------------------------
    private _loadData(): void { /* ... */ }
}
```

## Dependency Injection
**Use `inject()` function** instead of constructor injection:

```typescript
// Good - inject() syntax
export class MyComponent {
    private readonly router = inject(Router);
    private readonly http = inject(HttpClient);
    private readonly service = inject(MyService);
}

// Avoid - constructor injection
export class MyComponent {
    constructor(
        private router: Router,
        private http: HttpClient,
    ) {}
}
```

## Visibility Modifiers
**ALL properties MUST have explicit visibility:**

| Modifier | Use When |
|----------|----------|
| `private` | Internal logic only, not used in template |
| `protected` | Used in template or by child classes |
| `public` | Needs external access (rare) |

```typescript
private readonly router = inject(Router);        // Internal only
protected readonly items: Item[] = [];           // Used in template
public readonly apiUrl = 'https://...';          // External access needed
```

**Default to `private`** - only use `protected` when template needs access.

## Component Size
- **Keep components focused** - one responsibility per component
- **Extract when too large** - if scrolling becomes necessary, consider splitting
- **Self-contained blocks** - each component owns its logic, template, and styles
- **Avoid global styles** - prefer component-scoped styles
